WEBVTT

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:23.410
Boss, lookin' kinda happy there.

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:25.790
Not gonna watch?

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:30.450
The deal's for a full house on closing night.
We're leaving, Sakoda.

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:32.540
You're the boss, boss!

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.330
"Dictionary"

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:49.410
It's already show time.

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:53.580
It felt like the blink of an eye.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:59.410
The show might have some hiccups,
so back each other up if that happens.

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:01.500
I will if I can...

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:02.870
How are ticket sales?

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:07.080
We have some left, but we'll sell more
with positive audience reviews.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:12.500
Right! If we do our best for each show,
more people will come!

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:16.330
Yeah, that's why we put in
different twists every show.

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:19.160
We'll have them come many times.

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:21.700
We've got to make them want to come again.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:23.750
Just do it like we always do.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:24.910
Yeah!

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:29.370
Let's trust in our efforts and
in the director and give it our all!

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:33.500
You really sound like the lead.

00:01:34.790 --> 00:01:43.700
Welcome to Mankai Company Spring Troupe's
production of <i>Romeo and Julius</i>.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:45.410
Seats are pretty filled.

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:49.790
Please be reminded that
during today's performance,

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:53.330
--recording and photography are not permitted.
--I'm curious how it'll turn out.

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:55.450
Don't get the jitters.

00:01:55.450 --> 00:02:00.250
The performance will begin shortly.
Please have a seat and enjoy the show.

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:03.910
It's finally time.

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:05.910
Just gotta do it.

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:08.450
No regrets.

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:10.160
I'm shaking.

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:12.620
I'm so exited!

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:19.160
Only the actors can go on stage.
All I can do is pray.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:22.790
Everyone, get out there
and enjoy your first show!

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:24.370
Yeah!

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:20.000
Set in Verona, Italy,
where House Capulet and House Montague

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:23.580
are engaged in a long-standing feud.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:31.660
It's finally time. I will ask Rosaline
to the party today!

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:42.870
Excuse me, I'll take this lovely bouquet.

00:04:42.870 --> 00:04:48.580
A bouquet, please. Addressed to... Rosaline.

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:49.660
What?!

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:51.290
Who are you?

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:56.120
I'm Romeo! <i>I'll </i>ask my
beloved Rosaline to the party.

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:59.750
Beloved? Don't be absurd.

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:04.790
I, Julius, will ask Rosaline to the party.

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:13.500
Rosaline! Please accept these flowers!

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:18.200
No, <i>I </i>offer them.
I'm the one who paid for them!

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:22.950
Oh no...

00:05:22.950 --> 00:05:24.540
Got rejected, Romeo?

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:27.000
You were, too! What's your problem?

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:28.700
Say that again!

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:37.330
They meet as rivals in love.
After they resolve their conflicts,

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:40.870
they become best friends.

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:45.500
There's a whole world I don't know out there.

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:49.290
I want to see it with my own eyes someday.

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:53.830
If we share the same dream,
there's only one thing to do.

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:58.200
Let's go on a journey together, Julius.

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:02.620
We can ditch this cramped town
and travel the world.

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:07.660
You've got brawn, Romeo, and I've got brains.

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:11.000
If we put our heads together,
we can do anything.

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:19.830
You're right! Together, we can go anywhere!

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:27.950
Romeo and Julius meet again at a party
where they find out they're enemies.

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:33.660
Mercutio is the one who invites Romeo
to the party. I'm up now.

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:41.750
Why didn't I start acting earlier?

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:42.620
Huh?

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:47.080
I joined the drama club at school,
but when my youngest brother got a fever

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:51.500
when I stayed late for rehearsal once,
I decided it wouldn't work out.

00:06:52.790 --> 00:06:58.330
That was just an excuse, though,
and I probably could've found a way.

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:02.080
But I gave up so easily.

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:08.450
I blamed the family I love,
because I couldn't commit.

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:14.950
No more regrets!

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:17.410
Mercutio!

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:20.000
Romeo, are you heartbroken?

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:24.120
Don't worry about it.
There's plenty of fish in the sea.

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:27.080
Let's go to the party to take your mind off it.

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:36.870
Romeo... Montague? I don't believe it.
Are you really Romeo of House Montague?

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:41.450
Julius, are you really of House Capulet?

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:52.580
Any more and I take this as a declaration of war
against House Montague.

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:55.120
No... Julius!

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:57.290
Julius!

00:07:57.290 --> 00:07:58.870
Romeo!

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:02.450
Julius!

00:08:02.450 --> 00:08:04.370
Romeo!

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:11.700
Romeo, why do you have to be Romeo Montague?

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:14.000
Forsake your home and name, Julius.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:18.000
Don't we have an even grander dream to share?!

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:24.120
I can't. I can't forsake my family.

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:32.160
Romeo and Julius are in a pinch
and go to Friar Laurence for help.

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:33.620
Let's see...

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:39.330
I practiced the lines
I couldn't say countless times.

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:44.870
Tsuzuru kept adjusting the script for me
until the last minute for me.

00:08:45.950 --> 00:08:49.750
I will aid you. The seeds of strife
will be uprooted.

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:55.540
Good will come of it.
May God bless your journey.

00:08:57.870 --> 00:08:59.580
Montague, you say?!

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:04.080
Stop, Julius. There's no knowing
what will happen on a night such as this.

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:07.950
One day, Romeo,
the town's future will hinge upon you.

00:09:07.950 --> 00:09:11.700
I'm not fit for that role, but I'll back you up.

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:14.410
Montagues, greatest of all calamities!

00:09:14.410 --> 00:09:17.910
Their house is an affliction
that must one day be exterminated.

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:22.700
I worry for you, Romeo! I must protect you!

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:24.370
For Julius!

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:26.500
For Romeo!

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:44.120
Getting more serious for acting
than you are for video games, Itaru?

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:47.370
Not sure. Can't tell yet!

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:59.200
Mercutio!

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:03.290
Romeo...

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:11.620
Mercutio!

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:18.500
Romeo... the town's future will hinge upon...

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:20.410
How could this...

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:26.330
This is indeed the fate of House Montague.

00:10:32.910 --> 00:10:36.330
You can't change your fate.

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:43.870
Though Mercutio and Tybalt survived,

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:49.500
Romeo confessed all his crimes
and was sentenced to death.

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:53.080
I want to save Romeo. What should I do?

00:10:53.080 --> 00:10:57.000
You can fool everyone with
a potion that feigns death.

00:10:57.000 --> 00:11:00.580
Don't die before I return, Romeo!

00:11:00.580 --> 00:11:05.370
Julius set out in search of
a potion to feign death.

00:11:06.370 --> 00:11:10.950
Then, on the day of Romeo's execution...

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:16.200
Julius, sorry I couldn't keep
my promise to journey with you.

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:17.580
Julius?!

00:11:20.870 --> 00:11:22.830
Die, Romeo!

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:30.410
Why?! I thought we were best friends!

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:35.250
You are Romeo Montague of House Montague!

00:11:57.410 --> 00:12:00.330
I can feel their fierce energy.

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:12.910
Romeo!

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:14.870
Julius!

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:34.000
I'll wait where we agreed to meet.

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:36.080
That's enough.

00:12:39.370 --> 00:12:42.950
Julius, you came to pass this to me...

00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:02.830
Last scene now.

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:30.080
I'm not one for physical labor
in the first place.

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:32.790
I'm never climbing up a mountain again.

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:38.160
Sorry about that, Julius. I'll fetch
the potion ingredients for you next time.

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:42.410
How many times are we going to go through this?

00:13:42.410 --> 00:13:44.330
Come, Julius...

00:13:44.330 --> 00:13:46.540
Just as we promised that day.

00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:49.620
We'll travel the world!

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:10.830
That's applause, right?

00:14:10.830 --> 00:14:11.910
The crowd.

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:13.080
Amazing.

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:15.200
Like a storm.

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:16.950
Hey!

00:14:16.950 --> 00:14:20.080
Stop spacing. Curtain call!

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:23.080
Yes, ma'am!

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:06.580
Thank you very much!

00:15:11.790 --> 00:15:13.870
Thank you very much!

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:17.790
Thank you very much!

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:22.040
Thanks <i>so </i>much!

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:38.370
Today was great, too! My third time!

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:40.500
They changed their lines a little, huh?

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:42.290
You think they change them each show?

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:44.500
Can't wait for closing night!

00:15:45.330 --> 00:15:48.200
Hey guys, after this...

00:15:55.660 --> 00:16:01.500
What can I expect after consecutive
performances and late-night meetings?

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:04.500
Director! Yikes!

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:06.410
Huh? Is it morning?

00:16:06.410 --> 00:16:09.370
Cl-Cl-Cl-Cl-Cl-Clo--

00:16:09.370 --> 00:16:13.040
--Calm down, please! What happened?
--Clo-Clo-Clo-Clo-Clo-Clo-Clo--

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:20.370
Closing night is sold out!

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:21.200
Huh?

00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:25.040
Just sold the last one!

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:26.870
Hold out?

00:16:26.870 --> 00:16:29.450
Then the theater...

00:16:30.700 --> 00:16:35.370
Won't be destroyed. It's thanks to you all!

00:16:35.370 --> 00:16:37.620
Hooray!

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:41.410
Masumi, wake up! Closing night's sold out!

00:16:41.410 --> 00:16:43.330
So annoying.

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:46.250
We did it, Itaru!

00:16:47.200 --> 00:16:50.410
Sorry, I was too enthusiastic.

00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:53.370
No, it's fine. But get off.

00:16:53.370 --> 00:16:58.700
We have two days left until closing night.
Let's finish this out with no regrets!

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:01.580
--Yeah!
--I'll do my verily best!

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:10.500
Happened at today's show, huh?

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:12.790
You scared me. What are you talking about?

00:17:12.790 --> 00:17:15.450
It's no use playing numb.

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:20.160
I just twisted it a little.
I can get through another two days.

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:23.370
Don't tell Director or the others.

00:17:23.370 --> 00:17:27.750
Speak up if you can't go on. Promise me.

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:31.160
All right.

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:44.000
It's a full house!

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:47.620
Everybody has high expectations for you guys.

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:53.790
Comin' in!

00:17:53.790 --> 00:17:56.450
I came to watch, as agreed.

00:17:56.450 --> 00:17:59.200
It's a full house, as agreed.

00:17:59.200 --> 00:18:03.290
Seems so. I'll put a hold on demolition.

00:18:03.290 --> 00:18:05.080
I'm so glad.

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:08.950
However, there's no point
unless you can satisfy your audience.

00:18:08.950 --> 00:18:14.000
Securing regulars is a necessity to bring in
a stable revenue for the troupe.

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:17.200
--To do that, you must not only continue
to put on high quality performances,

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:18.120
--Here comes another lecture.
--To do that, you must not only continue
to put on high quality performances,

00:18:18.120 --> 00:18:19.500
--Here comes another lecture.
--but also generate new ideas
to keep your regulars entertain--

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:22.040
--It's instructive.
--but also generate new ideas
to keep your regulars entertain--

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:23.330
What's so funny?

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:27.790
It's nothing... Just that
you're surprisingly caring.

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:30.540
Let's go, Sakoda.

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:32.370
You're the boss, boss!

00:18:33.370 --> 00:18:35.500
The theater today...

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:39.120
...reminds me of the old days.

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:49.080
Mercutio!

00:18:51.540 --> 00:18:56.000
Romeo... the town's future will hinge upon--

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:57.790
How could this...

00:18:57.790 --> 00:19:01.580
This is indeed the fate of House Montague!

00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:05.290
This is where Tybalt falls.

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:12.250
He favored his foot.

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:19.580
Sorry, lower the curtain--

00:19:19.580 --> 00:19:21.750
Stop!

00:19:21.750 --> 00:19:26.200
Stop, Tybalt. The duel is over!

00:19:27.700 --> 00:19:29.120
That line...

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:32.160
Sakuya is ad-libbing.

00:19:32.160 --> 00:19:34.870
The show must go on.

00:19:34.870 --> 00:19:37.040
Lower your sword!

00:19:37.040 --> 00:19:40.660
I can't do that, Romeo Montague!

00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:42.790
What should we do?

00:19:42.790 --> 00:19:45.120
We'll continue.

00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:51.450
How many times are we going to go through this?

00:19:51.450 --> 00:19:53.620
Come, Julius...

00:19:53.620 --> 00:19:56.200
Just as we promised that day.

00:19:56.200 --> 00:19:59.200
We'll travel the world!

00:20:09.330 --> 00:20:12.910
Theater's freakin' awesome! That was sick!

00:20:12.910 --> 00:20:14.450
Passable.

00:20:14.450 --> 00:20:15.290
Was great.

00:20:15.290 --> 00:20:17.120
It was great!

00:20:17.120 --> 00:20:20.620
Well, the costumes were good.

00:20:20.620 --> 00:20:24.000
Wow, this is the loudest we've had.

00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:26.410
A standing ovation.

00:20:26.410 --> 00:20:28.950
I was worried for a second there!

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:34.370
Is your foot okay?

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.250
Itaru?!

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:38.660
Does it hurt that much?

00:20:38.660 --> 00:20:39.950
Call an ambulance.

00:20:39.950 --> 00:20:41.450
No...

00:20:43.410 --> 00:20:45.330
I'm just...

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:51.540
...filled with emotion
that I've never felt before.

00:20:52.830 --> 00:20:55.580
I'm just happy.

00:20:55.580 --> 00:21:00.750
If that's so, does that mean
you'll stay with the troupe?

00:21:04.370 --> 00:21:06.040
Guess so.

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:15.160
I'm sure...

00:21:17.790 --> 00:21:22.450
...that they'll remember this show
for the rest of their lives.

00:23:05.290 --> 00:23:07.040
What's got you looking so smug?

00:23:07.040 --> 00:23:09.330
Oh, Sakyo!

00:23:09.330 --> 00:23:15.910
You've gotta keep moving.
You only finished Spring Troupe's first show.

00:23:15.910 --> 00:23:19.700
So? Do you have potential members
for Summer Troupe?

00:23:19.700 --> 00:23:23.200
Well, we'll go recruit...

00:23:24.200 --> 00:23:27.830
...but there are also a few
I plan to reach out to.

00:23:37.040 --> 00:23:40.290
"Recruiting New Troupe Members"

00:23:40.290 --> 00:23:43.250
"Recruiting New Troupe Members"
Mankai Company, huh?
